@inject ClipboardService Clipboard
@inject INotificationService Notification

@*
    Browsers refuse to hand a page certain directories regardless of what the user picks. On Linux that
    blocklist covers everything under ~/.config - which is exactly where RetroArch keeps its saves by
    default, so this is the normal case for Linux users rather than an edge case.

    Nothing this app does can lift that: the refusal happens in the browser before the page is involved.
*@

<div class="folder-help">
    <h3 class="folder-help-title">If the browser refused your saves folder</h3>

    <p>
        Browsers keep a list of directories they will never hand to a web page. On Linux that list covers
        everything inside <code>~/.config</code> — which is where RetroArch stores saves by default, so
        <code>~/.config/retroarch/saves</code> can never be linked directly. The refusal happens in the
        browser before this page has any say in it.
    </p>

    <p>The fix is to keep your saves somewhere outside that list. Two ways:</p>

    <h4 class="folder-help-sub">1. Point RetroArch at a normal folder (recommended)</h4>
    <p class="muted">
        Permanent, and every save you make from then on lands somewhere linkable.
    </p>
    <pre class="folder-help-code">@MoveCommands</pre>
    <Button Size="@ButtonSize.Small" OnClick="() => Copy(MoveCommands)">Copy</Button>
    <p class="muted">
        Then in RetroArch: <strong>Settings → Directory → Save Files</strong>, and choose the new folder.
    </p>

    <h4 class="folder-help-sub">2. Symlink it</h4>
    <p class="muted">
        Less disruptive, but may not help: browsers resolve a symlink to its real location before checking
        it, so a link pointing into <code>~/.config</code> is usually refused too. Worth one try.
    </p>
    <pre class="folder-help-code">@SymlinkCommand</pre>
    <Button Size="@ButtonSize.Small" OnClick="() => Copy(SymlinkCommand)">Copy</Button>
</div>

@code {
    private const string MoveCommands =
        "mkdir -p ~/Games/PokemonSaves\n" +
        "cp -r ~/.config/retroarch/saves/. ~/Games/PokemonSaves/";

    private const string SymlinkCommand =
        "ln -s ~/.config/retroarch/saves ~/PokemonSaves";

    private async Task Copy(string text)
    {
        await Clipboard.WriteTextAsync(text);
        _ = Notification.Open(new()
        {
            Message = "Copied",
            NotificationType = NotificationType.Success,
        });
    }
}
